---
/* The seasonal overlay's top pieces: the two top corners and what hangs from
   one, the sky above the hero art, and a band of snow along the hero's top
   edge. Empty elements whose pictures come from `season.css`, which draws
   them only under `html[data-season]`, so a page with no season active
   fetches no picture and paints nothing here. The layer spans `main` and is
   placed from its top edge, which is the hero's, and every piece is put in
   space the hero leaves empty. Everything placed from an element's bottom or
   belonging to an element this component does not render -- the scene
   under the hero art, the header's, the sections' and the footer's pieces --
   is a pseudo-element in `season.css` instead. The classes name a place,
   not a picture: each season decides what stands there. */
import '../styles/season.css';
---

<div class="season-layer" aria-hidden="true">
	<i class="season-snow"></i>
	<i class="season-corner season-corner-start"></i>
	<i class="season-corner season-corner-end"></i>
	<i class="season-dangle"></i>
	<i class="season-sky"></i>
	<i class="season-flock"></i>
	<i class="season-flyer"></i>
</div>
